<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every user-facing string in the app.

  One file, on purpose. The strings here were inline literals at forty-odd call
  sites, which is fine until one of them needs changing: a wording fix becomes a
  hunt, and two sites drift into saying different things about the same control.
  A label that disagrees with itself is worse than an ugly one — the user cannot
  tell which is current.

  Two kinds of text are deliberately NOT here:

    - Log tags and diagnostic text the user never reads. Putting those in
      resources makes them look translatable, and they are not: they are for a
      logcat grep, and they name facts, not English.
    - The demo map's filename, which is debug output and appears in Diagnostics.

  Naming: <name> is the string's job, not its wording. `no_depth` survives a
  rewording; `no_depth_map_error_message` does not.
-->
